LEAPS
-----
The CTMC transport, the discrete Jarzynski log-weight, the locally equivariant rate-matrix
parametrization and the PINN objective follow

    P. Holderrieth, M. S. Albergo and T. Jaakkola, "LEAPS: A discrete neural sampler via locally
    equivariant networks", ICML 2025. https://github.com/malbergo/leaps

frogs/sampler.py, frogs/nets/transport.py, frogs/nets/free_energy.py and frogs/trainer.py are derived
from that reference implementation; consult its license before redistributing those portions.

Cluster expansions, metadynamics reference data and the SEGAL baseline
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The AgPd and CuAu effective cluster interactions and the metadynamics reference free energies in
data/reference/, and the SEGAL model reimplemented in baselines/segal/, are from

    J. Damewood, D. Schwalbe-Koda and R. Gomez-Bombarelli, "Sampling lattices in semi-grand
    canonical ensemble with autoregressive machine learning", npj Comput. Mater. 8, 61 (2022).
    https://github.com/learningmatter-mit/Segal

redistributed under the MIT License; the upstream notice is kept in data/reference/LICENSE-Segal.
